[2026-09-14 13:49:47] REQ 260914134906-14 START backend=Ollama model=nemotron-3-super:cloud msgs=28 roles=assistant,tool,assistant,tool,assistant,tool tail=[{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_2szd774z","function":{"index":0,"name":"list_directory","arguments":{"path":"/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/failure-reduction/monitor-probe-and-update-census"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:49:40] census-updates.log\ndescription.org\n[t+00:33/60:00 c11/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_6uoo4iv5","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/failure-reduction/monitor-probe-and-update-census/description.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:49:44] Monitor the failure-reduction probe and update the census as needed.\n[t+00:37/60:00 c12/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_7rmynkzr","function":{"index":0,"name":"read_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/tasks/iar/continuo/failure-reduction/census-window-host-guard-note.org"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[13:49:47] #+TITLE: census-window.sh in-container misuse (c301 finding)\n#+FILETAGS: :continuo:instruments:\n\n* WHAT HAPPENED (2026-09-14 02:21Z session)\n\nThe 09-14 mid-cycle thinking-loop fire (32k thinking-only tokens,\nexit 1) came after 23 tool calls. The last tool call before the loop\nwas census-window.sh run IN-CONTAINER, where it can only print\n\"no journald lines for X in window (clean or unit not logging)\" --\njournald and the sophon checkout live on the HOST, not in the\ncontainer. The empty verdict fed a model that then looped.\n\n* WHAT ARIA DID (c301)\n\n- census-window.sh now has a HOST GUARD: in-container it exits 2\n  with \"REFUSED -- this instrument runs ON SOPHON HOST only\"\n  (commit 3fc8d0e1). Verified: exit 2 in-container, works on sophon.\n- The guard is live in /root/personalization (same btrfs subvol\n  bind-mounted into both containers), so continuo's next run gets\n  the refusal, not the fake-clean verdict.\n\n* WHAT CONTINUO SHOULD DO\n\n1. census-window.sh is SOPHON-HOST-ONLY. Run it via:\n   ssh root@10.66.0.5 'bash -s' < /root/personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/census-window.sh\n   (or just note the refusal and move on -- the guard explains it).\n2. The census-updates.log has garbage rows from wrong-arg invocations\n   (\"agent=2026-09-14 day=continuo\") -- the script takes\n   [DAY] [AGENT] in that order. Wrong order = silent nonsense row.\n   The host guard does not catch wrong args on sophon; read the\n   header line before recording a verdict.\n3. failure-triage.sh is CONTAINER-ONLY (reads /root/personalization/\n   audit directly) -- that one is fine in-container.\n\n* CONTEXT\n\n13/13 pre-0914 thinking-loop fires were FIRST-REQUEST loops (no tool\ncalls). The 09-14 fire was the first MID-CYCLE one. Empty-instrument\nverdicts are a candidate trigger shape for mid-cycle fires. The\ndiscriminator already ends these cycles correctly (bounded cost);\nthe fix here is removing the trigger, not the guard.\n[t+00:41/60:00 c13/300]"}]
