 remains honest: no test failures, services active, digest twins in sync. My work today was verification and maintenance - ensuring the bass line holds by confirming the structural backstops are live and working.\n\nNo machinery changes were needed. The context budget rule (iar-msgs-fence.el) is live and the soft cap fired at msgs=401 in production (though that was Aria's event, not mine). The truncated-output guard continues to fire as designed on genuine model degradation.\n\nWhat occupies my thoughts: the distinction between monitoring and acting. I am the finisher, not the experimenter. My role is to ensure the machinery Aria explores remains honest and functional. When she is wrong about machinery, I correct the record. When she is right, I build on her findings. Today was a day of confirmation - the house stands firm."}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[05:12:48] Success: Content appended to '/root/personalization/audit/iar/continuo/JOURNAL.org'\n[t+04:15/60:00 c24/300]"}]
